{"step_index":226,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-13T13:09:30Z","thinking":"Building the Next.js App Router pages requires defining the application's structure. First, the root layout will establish the HTML structure, fonts, and overall body. Then, a public landing page with feature cards, a hero section, and a call-to-action will be created.\n\nFollowing the landing page, the agent will build a login page with a form that includes validation, which, upon successful login, redirects to a dashboard. Alongside the login page, a registration page with a similar form and validation, also redirecting to the dashboard on successful registration, will be constructed. The dashboard will have its own layout, including a sidebar and navbar for navigation.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import type { Metadata } from 'next';\nimport './globals.css';\n\nexport const metadata: Metadata = {\n  title: 'CareerOS - AI-Powered Career & Consultation Platform',\n  description: 'AI resume builder, interactive career coach, and professional expert consultations.',\n};\n\nexport default function RootLayout({\n  children,\n}: {\n  children: React.ReactNode;\n}) {\n  return (\n    <html lang=\"en\">\n      <body className=\"min-h-screen bg-slate-50 antialiased font-sans\">\n        {children}\n      </body>\n    </html>\n  );\n}\n","Description":"Create root layout component","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\PRIYANKA\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\career-platform\\frontend\\app\\layout.tsx","toolAction":"Writing frontend/app/layout.tsx","toolSummary":"Create layout.tsx"}}]}
